<title>USA: Conrail confirms meetings with AFL-CIO.</title>
<headline>Conrail confirms meetings with AFL-CIO.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Conrail and CSX Corp issued a statement Wednesday confirming that meetings have begun with the Transportation Trades Department of the AFL-CIO to discuss the proposed merger between the two companies.</p>
<p>The statement said Tuesday's meeting established channels of communication and further discussions are expected as the merger proceeds.</p>
<p>The AFL-CIO previously announced it had formed a coalition of rail unions to analyze the merger and develop a formal position.</p>
<p>A federal court Tuesday paved the way for the proposed multibillion-dollar merger by denying rival railroad company Norfolk Southern Corp's request to block the deal.</p>
</text>
